=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free union +
  catalogs + parse/projection + registration + diagnostics, unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the
  cache-then-network data port), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (the ObservableObject state holder) and <Name>.cs (the
  Fluent view). The generated prompt's idealized "TriggerConfigurator.xaml + TriggerConfiguratorViewModel.cs
  under TeslaSync/Features/Automations" is mapped onto these real conventions — exactly as the peer automations
  surfaces ConditionBuilder (feature-views/ConditionBuilder/*) and AutomationActivityFeed already are. The C#
  namespace is TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Automations, so the surface is logically under "Automations" as the
  prompt's Output column intends.
- This unit is a controlled sub-form, not a routed page: the web source is a component that takes props
  (trigger / onChange) and renders one kind selector + the kind-specific body; manifest route is (unrouted). The
  native TriggerConfigurator is therefore a ContentControl whose ViewModel raises TriggerChanged (web onChange);
  it is unrouted, so there is no NavigationView / ShellPageFactory entry to add (the conditional "if routed"
  requirement does not apply) — the peer automations sub-forms are wired the same way.
- Manifest models one data source — useGeofences (GET /geofences). It is bound through the P1/S8 state-holder
  seam: TriggerConfigurator.Source.cs (ITriggerGeofenceSource / TriggerGeofenceSource) runs a single
  cache-then-network read of GET /geofences through the shared CacheThenNetworkEngine and projects each JSON
  emission into a tolerant TriggerGeofence list, preserving lifecycle status / freshness / error; the
  TriggerConfiguratorViewModel folds those emissions into a TriggerGeofenceLoadState (loading / loaded / empty /
  error / stale / offline). The view never performs HTTP (ADR-004). The geofence operation id resolves through
  the generated client (Operations.Locations.Geofences).
- The four web branches are reproduced verbatim by the WinUI-free Model union + the view's BuildBody switch:
  trigger_schedule (TimePicker + weekday ToggleButtons in simple mode, or a cron TsInput in advanced mode, plus
  the mode toggle and a timezone TsSelect — web buildCronExpr/parseCronExpr/handleDayToggle reproduced in
  TriggerCron), trigger_event (event TsSelect over VEHICLE_EVENTS), trigger_geofence (geofence TsSelect +
  transition TsSelect + conditional dwell NumberBox), trigger_signal (signal + operator TsSelect, a
  bool/text/number value editor, and the "fire on any change" TsToggle — web signalValueFromInput reproduced in
  TriggerSignalCatalog/SignalTrigger). createDefaultTrigger, SIGNAL_FIELD_OPTIONS/BOOL_FIELD_KEYS, DAYS and
  COMMON_TIMEZONES are ported and asserted headlessly.
- 3 data states for the one source: loading -> TsSkeleton + LiveRegion announce (BuildGeofenceLoading); empty ->
  TsEmptyState (BuildGeofenceEmpty, the manifest "empty" state); success/loaded -> populated TsSelect
  (BuildGeofenceSelect, the manifest "success" state). Beyond the two manifest-declared states the surface also
  renders error (TsQueryError + Retry, attempt count) and the >2 min staleness / offline freshness chips
  (TsDataFreshness / offline Caption) per ADR-013 — never a blank region.
- Strings: all 21 web i18n keys resolve through the ILocalizer facade with the web key names (the codebase's
  dominant bare-key convention, matching the peer ConditionBuilder and the acceptance criterion "key names match
  web"); en/ar/he Resources.resw carry translation.<key> rows for all 21. The single previously-absent row,
  translation.automations.builder.cronHint, was added to all three catalogs (21/21/21) with the verbatim web
  default "minute hour day-of-month month day-of-week" (the web key is itself absent from web/src/i18n/en.json
  and rendered from the t() fallback, so the value matches what the web shows in every locale).
- a11y: the surface root, the kind-selector grid, every ToggleButton/TimePicker/TsSelect/NumberBox/TsToggle and
  the geofence label carry an AutomationProperties name; the loading branch announces via LiveRegion; the
  freshness/offline glyphs are decorative. The only motion is the shared TsFadeIn entrance, which honours
  reduce-motion by construction. PII-safe diagnostics emit only "view.opened" — never a trigger value, signal,
  geofence name or cron expression. SI units N/A on this surface (no unit-bearing fields; dwell minutes and the
  cron clock are bare scheduling integers, not SI-converted quantities).

